     5	Read before the manuscript: `EDITION_BRIEF.md`; all of `OWNER-DECISIONS.md`, with special attention to #18, #23–#25, #33, #42 and #46–#51; Book 7's `BOOK_MAP.md`, all eight AFTER MOVEMENT blocks and binding coordinator rulings in `STATE_LEDGER.md`, `protected-patterns.txt`, and `COMPLETION-PLAN.md`; Book 6 ch59–60; Book 8's opening plan; and Book 6's whole-arc read as the report model. Then read `manuscript/chapter-01.md` through `chapter-60.md` in order, every word, keeping `state/completion/whole-arc-notes.md` during the read. Mechanical audits followed: calendar, deployments, money, board, sheets, injuries, geography, quotations, knowledge releases, protected text, repetition, formula metrics, and the required source probe. No manuscript file was modified and no git command was run.
     6	
     7	## Verdict
     8	
     9	**PASS — RATIFY.** The book holds as a complete novel. It begins by making freedom from institutional measurement feel materially true: the board records deeds, not rank, and Cael can write `I'm free` without irony (ch7:27–103, :269–295). It then makes that freedom morally insufficient. Quiet ground turns his old absence into unique power (ch27:181–239; ch29:243–309), the Ring lets him become the only effective practitioner in the party (ch31:211–289; ch32:139–301), and he uses that advantage to take from Oryn without consent (ch36:65–225; ch37:141–240). The second half does not absolve him. It builds a rule through refusal, explicit permission, repayment and restraint (ch38:103–229; ch47:97–129; ch48:7–105; ch55:221–287; ch56:153–205). The ending therefore earns both claims at once: nobody out here can reduce him to an instrument, and the place where only he works still requires other people, their boundaries and their evidence (ch58:219–229; ch60:31–41, :247–265).
    10	
    11	The calendar, deployment count, money, injuries, site geometry, names, knowledge limits, protected wording, Reader Standard and both book seams hold. Movements 3 and 7 earn their excess over the planning guide. The Hall adds a new opponent rule and a new cooperative solution rather than proving the Ring again (ch53:229–339; ch54:91–107, :191–323). The source-distance audit finds no surviving unprotected source-shaped passage. No line-level correction is warranted. The only recommended work is a controlled two-lane same-author texture pass: the book's hand/count/accounting motifs are appropriate, but its retrospective glosses, measured pauses and repeated evaluative looks make the surface more patterned than the events require.
    12	
    13	## 1. Continuity
    14	
    15	### Calendar, season and units — holds
    16	
    17	The required dates are exact: shelf day 2 (ch1:3–7); Lowmarch day 9 (ch2:3); ford day 53 (ch9:317; ch10:3–9); mountain days 70–84 (ch15:1–7; ch22:323–331); Fallow days 94–96 (ch27:157–183; ch28:67–105; ch30:237); long reading day 100 (ch36:233–279; ch38:77–87); birthday day 102 (ch40:3–5, :189–209); Oryn north day 111 (ch44:225–261; ch45:3–15); Millrace day 113 (ch47:3–25, :121–153); Stair days 114–115 (ch49:3–19; ch52:3–21, :355–359); Hall day 119 (ch54:3–15; ch55:153–165); first snow day 129 (ch59:121–139; ch60:31); last ferry day 130 (ch60:47–95); Oryn's letter day 131 (ch60:219–225).
    18	
    19	Manuscript-wide search found no season name, calendar month name or order, English weekday name, or metric unit. Generic `season` and `month` occur only in allowed senses (ch1:269; ch33:93; ch60:31). `Fathom by fathom` is a non-metric rope measure at ch60:91, not a violation.
    20	
    21	### Deployments and fragment rules — holds
    22	
    23	Every deployment log is monotonic: none through day 52 (ch1:3; ch9:317); one after the ford through the Fallow approach (ch11:419; ch27:239); thirteen after the Ring (ch33:223; ch46:195); fourteen after the first consented Tide read (ch48:281); twenty-three after the Stair (ch51:217; ch53:389); twenty-six after the Hall (ch55:163); and twenty-seven after the second consented Tide read, including the closing inventory (ch55:301; ch60:31). Practice, involuntary Path use and non-field tests are explicitly kept outside Cael's deployment definition (ch1:269; ch19:257–277; ch29:243–309; ch39:245–249).
    24	
    25	The fragment mechanics do not drift. Iron reads air or body, never both (ch4:97); Storm lanes bill ten, ten and twelve and clear at eleven, eleven and thirteen (ch4:97; ch32:215; ch51:47); Wind locks the landing for one count (ch4:85; ch32:163; ch51:21–33); Anchor is sure at ten feet, faint at twelve and absent at fourteen (ch4:99; ch50:261–293); Compression acts at contact (ch4:91; ch51:51–59); Ember remains one point (ch32:47; ch51:73–83, :213); Blade remains partial (ch4:101); Tide remains self-and-contact and governed by the body's owner (ch38:39; ch48:17–23, :73–105; ch60:37).
    26	
    27	Shadow is used exactly twice, at the Ring and Stair (ch32:117–127; ch50:213–255). Both uses are outside hostile sight; Oryn sees neither and never learns Seln is the source (ch34:25–47; ch51:165–173). The closing inventory states the same sealed logic without expanding it (ch60:37).
