    29	### Money, board, bolts and sheets — holds
    30	
    31	The Lowmarch sale becomes a sealed reserve that never enters the working purse (ch3:101–137; ch7:269–279). Working cash proceeds coherently through 52 after the ford jobs (ch14:337–451), 116 after Oxhollow (ch21:345–361; ch22:323–329), 108 after the cart debt (ch24:233–251), 102 after the birthday room and kid (ch40:23–37, :383–389), and 96 after the cold-term paper room (ch60:3–13, :29–31). The Stair's 300 stays `taken; not paid` and never enters the purse (ch59:161–175).
    32	
    33	The crew reaches the wall thirteenth, then tenth, then eleventh; Pike's final book has nine lines, leaves the rating blank, and the cloth still says eleventh (ch7:183–229; ch25:3–49; ch45:105–165; ch59:175–217; ch60:29–31). Brom recovers five bolts from the Ring while the sixth remains on its floor (ch34:113–151; ch35:15–23). The sheet count closes at eleven Ring, twenty-nine Stair and twelve Hall, fifty-two total (ch57:13–17; ch60:19–25).
