    36	
    37	Lira's right ankle never mends; it remains taped and flat-footed through first snow (ch11:297–311; ch35:79–81; ch43:137–143; ch58:17–27; ch59:23–45). Oryn mends the tibia, not the ankle (ch20:205–263; ch21:155–207). The left forearm remains in its sling and is not silently released when snow comes (ch33:91–119; ch42:79–125; ch58:17–27).
    38	
    39	Cael's calf reopens on mountain and Ring and closes by day 99; his ribs are retaped, later billed by the Hall, cold-aggravated, and quiet by day 129 (ch19:151–159; ch20:27–35; ch34:149–177; ch35:265–271; ch54:139–175; ch55:89–103; ch59:19–21, :47–49). Brom's one hand has four finger-pad cuts, his right shoulder takes the bolt and then the Hall reopening, and every treatment carries forward (ch34:113–151; ch49:237–273; ch51:125–153; ch54:139–175; ch55:25–45; ch56:33–67). Karis's hand and throat remain impaired until their staged recoveries; her mountain emptying is reserve exhaustion, not an untracked wound (ch19:125–173; ch20:41–53; ch34:113–137; ch35:241–251). Oryn's reserve is repeatedly priced and is full again only after three days without mending (ch34:179–225; ch47:43–85; ch51:125–153; ch60:109–119).
