   212	
   213	*Job, Hirer, Witness, Outcome, Price.*
   214	
   215	He looked for the sixth, though he knew that it was not there, having counted five; he looked for it all the same, the way you look for a stair in the dark, with a foot. Every book that had ever had his name in it had kept a place for what he was. There had been a column in a district office at the far end of the country with one word in it, and a narrow column with no heading in a station's register, and a line on a form where a registrar had hunted two years for a better word and written *unclassified*. His foot came down on nothing at all, and the jolt of it went through him.
