+# Book 7 — *Void Roads*: listening-proof running notes, part 1
+
+Scope: `manuscript/chapter-01.md` through `chapter-15.md`. Each chapter is read in full, in order, from a complete numbered printout. Scene counts below count the text sections separated by `---` (therefore breaks + 1). First/last six-word witnesses preserve punctuation and markdown exactly as printed.
+
+## Chapter 1 — The Valley With No Name
+
+Five scenes.
+
+1. First six: `*Second day past the Line. One`  
+   Last six: `had finished with her second boot.`  
+   Listening notes: Clear Cael/Brom/Lira attribution; Karis and sleeping Seln are introduced before either can be confused with a speaker. Italic opening count and the nine-fragment inventory need document register; `Deployment since the Line: none` is words, not a visual numeral. `lead` in “lead shoulder” does not occur; `read` forms are clear by syntax. Clean.
+2. First six: `They finished the hill by hand.`  
+   Last six: `nobody had told them anything yet.`  
+   Listening notes: Lira/Karis tree-name exchange alternates cleanly; Brom’s track and fire-ring findings are tagged. Karis’s italic field note should flatten as written text, with `L.` spoken as the letter. Distances and counts are spelled out. Clean.
+3. First six: `On the fourth day the river`  
+   Last six: `*Deployment since the Line: none.*`  
+   Listening notes: The unnamed courier is consistently “the woman”; no competing unnamed woman speaks. Her `Hm.` is an audible acknowledgment. The two italic log paragraphs are distinct from dialogue; no numeral or attribution stumble. Clean.
+4. First six: `Below the ford it began to`  
+   Last six: `it, which is right. He would.*`  
+   Listening notes: `wind` in the grass is WIND; the forms of `read` are unambiguous. Seln identifies himself inside the long quiet exchange before the untaged short replies; Cael/Seln alternation remains clear. The closing italic log includes the deployment line inside one entry and should keep its document cadence. Clean.
+5. First six: `They came up with the carts`  
+   Last six: `feet. Nobody anywhere lit a thing.`  
+   Listening notes: The unnamed old man, boy and woman remain distinct by role and action. The old man’s protected “paper” exchange is attributable. Council speech after Cael’s `Hold` is tagged or unmistakable by content; Karis’s correction from three to four fires is clear. The italic day/ruling line is a log entry. Clean.
+
+## Chapter 2 — Fourteen Slips
+
+Five scenes.
+
+1. First six: `They walked behind the three carts`  
+   Last six: `the drum began to creak again.`  
+   Listening notes: Cael/Seln/Lira/Brom exchanges are tagged and distinct. `read` in “he read it” is RED; `wind` turning leaves is WIND. All quantities are spelled out. Clean.
+2. First six: `Nobody told them where to stand`  
+   Last six: `dark coat anywhere in the meadow.`  
+   Listening notes: The standing-money boy is the only speaking unnamed boy and is distinguished from the ferry boy by the narrator’s explicit comparison. Karis’s observational finding and the council’s replies are attributable. Clean.
+3. First six: `It was a ship's plank.`  
+   Last six: `back," said a voice behind them.`  
+   Listening notes: Fourteen posted slips are italic document text and should be voiced as separate board entries. Potential narrator defect at line 127: the visual abbreviation-and-digit example `*Cu 3*` will likely be read as “C U three,” although the intended spoken form is “Copper Three”; hold as a required-fix candidate. Lira/Cael alternation is clear, and Pike’s entrance is intentionally identified only in the next scene. 
+4. First six: `He was sixty, or a little`  
+   Last six: `or don't. I'm at my dinner."`  
+   Listening notes: Pike is established before speaking. His five-column heading is italic document text; the commas supply usable pauses. The name-giving run identifies each voice by narration, and Seln’s delayed answer is explicit. Pike’s repeated looks are deliberate characterization. `read` forms are clear. Clean.
+5. First six: `They had a fire that night,`  
+   Last six: `he liked the answer no better.`  
+   Listening notes: Five-person fire conversation stays attributable by tags and Path/rank content. Lira’s `*Wind. Iron, Rank One.*`, Karis’s italic `*Outcome.*`, Cael’s full log and the repeated deployment line need written-text register. Clean apart from the held line-127 candidate.
+
+## Chapter 3 — What the Board Pays
+
+Five scenes.
+
+1. First six: `Brom laid it out for them`  
+   Last six: `that can't walk in a circle."`  
+   Listening notes: Brom’s grain demonstration is easy to follow by action and tags; Seln’s interjection is named immediately. Karis’s gelding-name question and Lira/Brom replies remain distinct. Clean.
+2. First six: `The ferryman was a long sour`  
+   Last six: `on her hip, outside her coat.`  
+   Listening notes: The unnamed ferryman remains distinct from the ferry boy; Lira and Brom are tagged through the horse sale. No homograph or figure is ambiguous. Clean.
+3. First six: `They sealed the money that night,`  
+   Last six: `"Five," said Brom. "I'm greedy."`  
+   Listening notes: Reserve arithmetic is all in words and the sealed sum is deliberately not voiced. Five-way agreement is attributable; Seln’s `Mm` should remain audible. Clean.
+4. First six: `The slip with the seal on`  
+   Last six: `yet. I've never weighed one before."`  
+   Listening notes: Broker, ferry boy and party voices are distinct. During the tree strike, Cael’s inward italic `*Hold*` is thought, not a document; Pressure/Storm/Wind are Path fragments. `wind` does not occur as a homograph here. Brom’s suppression of Iron Skin is clear. Clean.
+5. First six: `The ferryman made his mark on`  
+   Last six: `I don't remember putting it there."`  
+   Listening notes: Pike’s aloud ledger line is clearly introduced, repeated, and projected to the meadow; the woman at the pan does not answer. Italic outcome terms, board descriptions and Cael’s closing log need document register. `Teague` is a written one-word heading here. Deployment remains `none`; the four offered abilities are explicitly not deployments. Clean.
+
+## Chapter 4 — The Hold
+
+Six scenes.
+
+1. First six: `He began with Lira, because she`  
+   Last six: `had turned and set her feet.`  
+   Listening notes: Training voices stay distinct by named focus and tags. Counts and distances are words. `Fifth-day` is the allowed house weekday. Clean.
+2. First six: `He had told three people what`  
+   Last six: `she said. "It pays two marks."`  
+   Listening notes: Cael’s complete nine-fragment inventory and deployment line are protected italic log text: flatten without emphasis, but retain one-entry-per-paragraph cadence. `the read` is REED; `Wind` is the Path noun; `Gold` is the tier. Lira’s interruption after the log is clearly identified. Clean.
+3. First six: `The fence was a day up`  
+   Last six: `and went to fetch the brands.`  
+   Listening notes: The steading’s unnamed old man is the only unnamed speaker; the later first-person note is Karis’s italic field entry. `bowshot` has BOH. Clean.
+4. First six: `They set the last post on`  
+   Last six: `Rent. Deployment since the Line: none.*`  
+   Listening notes: The old man’s `Cheap` is explicitly interpreted by Lira and Brom without confusing the speaker. Metal `lead` in “the river turned from brass to lead” is LED; flag for pronunciation direction, not a text defect. Seln/Cael dusk exchange is tagged. The italic closing log stays one document segment. Clean.
+5. First six: `Seln took the cold road on`  
+   Last six: `waiting, and did not altogether mind.`  
+   Listening notes: Seln POV is established immediately. The italic internal report is remembered form language, not spoken dialogue; `*Nothing further to report*` continues it. `wind` is WIND. Clean.
+6. First six: `A boy brought the slip in`  
+   Last six: `have told me that at Fenmark."`  
+   Listening notes: Slip text is visually written and introduced before the unnamed hide-woman reappears; she is clearly identified by the barley-cake callback. Fight orders from Brom and Karis are tagged. Cael’s `*There?*` / `*Wheel. Hers. Leave it.*` is inward fragment dialogue. `bowstring` is BOH. No deployment occurs. Clean.
+

