   413	He could have stood behind that white muzzle himself. He owned the means, and at dusk Shadow had been all but lifting his feet for him; nobody on that gravel would have had to go down thirty yards in the open and land locked, and there would be no holes in his leg tonight. He had chosen the loud thing, in front of a witness, and taken the bite, and it was the first time since he left the hill that the seal had sent him a bill.
