   420	
   421	He had written the other word some fifty times, and he had expected the new one to look like a stain on the page. It did not. All those weeks he had supposed that the *none* was the thing he was guarding; but it had been more like a purse kept shut, so that there should be something in it on the one evening when it was wanted. He had opened it once, for one deployment, and counted out what the thing cost, and shut it again.
