+4. First six: `He was sixty, or a little`  
+   Last six: `or don't. I'm at my dinner."`  
+   Listening notes: Pike is established before speaking. His five-column heading is italic document text; the commas supply usable pauses. The name-giving run identifies each voice by narration, and Seln’s delayed answer is explicit. Pike’s repeated looks are deliberate characterization. `read` forms are clear. Clean.
+5. First six: `They had a fire that night,`  
