editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:147:"How deep?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:185:"Is that wrong?" said Lira, from the cart.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:213:"Should they be?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:333:Under it he had five things. Three carts had gone a day without a word, and every one of their people wore an edge outside the coat, the boy included. There were rings of stones on the halting-grounds that had never been burned in, because they had never been meant for fire. A courier had counted their smokes from a ridge and told them it was their wood. And a boy had been about to show them something, and had had it taken out of his hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:351:"And if a wheel goes down in a river?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-01.md:361:"And you?" said Lira, looking at him. "You've nine fragments, and not one of them's a Path. Does it count?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:47:"A third what?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:109:"Is five enough?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:243:"What does he want?" said Lira. She was sitting on the gravel with her boots off, wringing out a stocking.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:275:"Two hours of what?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:293:"Is that all you're going to say?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-08.md:297:"Seven what?" said Karis. She had her pencil ready, and her voice was not altogether steady.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:77:"What for?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:105:"Give what one?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:231:"Where?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-11.md:295:"Is there a healer?" said Cael. "Anywhere in reach?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-07.md:49:"Why twice?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-07.md:117:"Clearance of what?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-07.md:123:"What's HOLD?" said Lira, across the plank.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-07.md:287:He had been turning one sentence over since a frame-house door, and he had not written it, because he had not been sure that it would stand. He had waited to see whether the country would take it back, and it had had forty-nine days in which to do so. He put the pencil to the page.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-04.md:101:*Blade, from Ephram. Partial still. It asks "Edge?" of anything with a corner on it, takes a name, and settles.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-04.md:289:"Before what water?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:29:"What's a high traverse?" said Lira. "In a carter's mouth. I know what it is on a hill."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:43:"What does he call a map?" she said. "I've a registry sheet in the middle box with the whole continent on it, printed, and a calfskin that a carter drew for his own wheels. They aren't the same kind of thing. Which does he want?"
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:73:"Does it need the cart?" he said. "We've none. We could walk your bench and measure it. She has a cord, and I can pace a yard."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:83:"What's up there?" said Lira. "Besides a shelf."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:133:"A day?" said Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:169:"What's that?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:187:Seln lit the fire with his flint. It was the fourth they had had on a road, and Cael noticed that not one of them watched the first smoke go up; the thing had become ordinary in twelve days, and he thought that a carter with cold feet would have been glad to see it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:191:"What goes in that?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:219:"Who came up here?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:253:"Can it be done?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-13.md:325:"Can I have one of those?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:23:"How did that get here?" said Lira, at his shoulder. "There's nothing on it. There's no town on it."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:89:"Is it wrong?" said Pike.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:129:"Has he been in?" said Cael. "The one at the top."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:135:"And said what?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:149:"Is he angry?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:159:"Who pays the four?" said Karis.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:171:He leaned over the curb, which smelled of wet stone and of nothing else, and he supposed that that was what was wrong with it.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:183:"What does it say?" said Brom.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:187:"How do you get it out?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:285:"How many?" said Brom. He was holding up his right hand.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:413:"Then why the cloth?" said Lira.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-14.md:459:"What's coming?" said Cael.

