editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:24:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — the telling and its cost (Reader Standard), binding.]** Movement 5 ends with Cael having taken the tenth fragment in Oryn's long reading without telling her first, and telling her the minute it was over. The edition treats that as a wrong done knowingly; the companions named it so and he agreed. This movement's first scene must therefore give Oryn full agency: SHE names what was done to her, in her own terms; she establishes whether and how the taking touched her; and she sets conditions and a cost that Cael cannot pay in advance out of his own ledger (the plan's "self first, ask first, tell her" is HER condition, stated by her, not offered by him). He does not argue his reasons, is not forgiven on the page for having confessed, and consent is not supplied after the fact. The acquisition stands and is not undone. Sources are told to her by Path, not by person, except the three she has touched; Seln is not identified as the source of Shadow-adjacent.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/packets/MOVEMENT-006.md:26:> **[Coordinator note 2026-10-11 — NO-SOURCE drafting, binding.]** Draft WITHOUT opening any source chapter under `books/`. The source-chapter references in the line below are retained for the coordinator's and reviewers' tools only; the author does not read them. Events come from this packet, `BOOK_MAP.md` (the plan sections, the protected-text section and the reserved-truths section) and `STATE_LEDGER.md`. Write `EVENT-LIST.md` first. Where a protected unit is quoted in the plan only in part, leave `[[TIER-B: <unit> — coordinator to supply protected text]]` and write around it. [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: coordinator O3]
