editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:100:The source (≈118,400) is retold at roughly equal weight, plus ≈181,600 of new room. Every item serves the book promise (*make the reader feel the edge territories as the first place Cael has ever been fully free — and then make that freedom complicated*) or the arc (*no instrument out here reads me* → *nothing out here reads me, and the oldest thing out here stops every live Arbiter but leaves my fragments answering*). [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit B4, B7] Nothing below changes an end state or opens a reserved truth.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:103:2. **The compressed roads and recoveries put on the page (+38,000).** The source summarizes the six days in the fin's lee and on the mountain's lip (+4k); the four days down to Oxhollow (+4k); the six days Oxhollow→Lowmarch (+4k); days 60–69 at Lowmarch and the well on the south road (+8k); the two days stone→Thornwater with Lira flat-footed (+3k); Thornwater→Lowmarch in the first cold (+2k); the three-day bearing walk (+4k); and the six days from the fourth site home in first snow (+5k). Thornwater's three stays get texture as a place that becomes home (+4k). *Why:* the arc's freedom is made of walking and of places that feed them, and the source keeps cutting it to a sentence.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:104:3. **The six-week skip and the first contracts on the page (+16,000).** The courier at the ford; falling in behind carters; Lowmarch's first week; the cart, the horse and the purse resolved (C1); the ferry escort, the fence-line and the wash as three short episodes; the meadow. *Why:* the source does all of this in a log. The edition's opening has to show the freedom before it complicates it, and to teach the board as a system.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:110:9. **Retelling weight (+9,000).** The source's own scenes, rewritten at the formula's paragraph rhythm and given air, with no new events.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:143:| **Oryn** | 9,200 (3.1%) | M3: 2,600 (Oxhollow's gate north, days 84–92: the hand she owed, the child three stops on, "a patient I want to read whole"; she puts a day on the route) · M6: 2,000 (day 100, the stool after the telling, the book on her knee: being a patient's source) · M6: 1,800 (days 111–112, the road north after leaving her mule with the crew; ends before Millrace's table) · M8: 2,800 (days 122–~128, the gap to Thornwater, the old woman's knee, writing the letter; ends on its four lines) | Her route, its arithmetic and debts; her city and why she left; her hands' findings; from day 100, the mechanism as told; the line's rule, which she tested alone; what she felt in him | Any theory of what he is or why the Quiet does not touch him ("I'm a healer, not a theorist"); the still place before he tells her (day 120); the content of Karis's hypothesis; anything about the Compact beyond what was said at a table; any sentimental declaration — her register breaks once, at the Hall, in Cael's POV |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:147:| **Lira** | 7,600 (2.5%) | M2: 1,800 (day 53, the bar at dusk without Wind: fast, with nothing at the end) · M3: 1,800 (day 78, the ledge: the burst her body chose; "That was me. The loud thing.") · M5: 2,000 (days 97–98: one arm, the order, "Later" kept; walking flat-footed because Oryn said) · M6: 2,000 (the bowman's lessons: shooting braced, one-armed, with a bow somebody else spans) | Everything she knows (the log, the fragments); her Fenmark and Norhold history; her want; her body's counts | Why Cael's fragments work inside before he tells her (day 110); any escalation of Cael–Lira past what the source shows (warmth and covenant, not declaration); asking for the ankle twice |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:162:| Karis | A primary source in a country that keeps nothing; a finding that outlives her | Refuses a second point under attack; the barn-table library; not asking the carter's wife; the lattice line across the mountain; the perimeter procedure; the wall of ignition from her knees; names the Quieting; stops her pen on the hypothesis; "I would go alone"; copies the wall she kneels on; the line and the argument | 18 |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:193:| **The anomaly → the still place** | M1–M5: "Still open. Still real. Patience." M6: the three words retired, with the reason. M8: a location. **Not a fragment; never counted; not the Quiet** | No theory, name-as-explanation, or *before/source/primordial* |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:220:Every winning mechanism is taught before it is used: discharge sense (ford → Ring); flight (herd day → stampede); the line (perimeter trials → Ring, Stair); Anchor unbinding (edition B6 ch31/ch33/ch38 → Stair) [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit C1]; strike-what-stays (afternoon → Hall). Each win is writable as *X removed Y's ability to Z* (source checkpoint). The opponent learns: the pack at the ford stops testing silent bodies; the rim waits instead of entering.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:230:**This source's own measured baseline** (`python3 editions/monroe-1.3/tools/formula_metrics.py` over the 24 chapters, 2026-10-01): sentence mean 15.4, **median 8**, **38.6% ≤5 words**, **10.2% ≥40 words**, paragraph median 34 (mean 49.5), **words per marked scene ≈615**, FRE 89.6, grade 4.6. Read: the source is *bimodal*, with too many fragments and too many very long accumulating sentences, and too few mid-length ones. Its paragraphs are long, its section breaks frequent and its reading level low. **The retelling's corrections, in order:** (1) shorten paragraphs (break on every turn of thought; the logs as short paragraphs); (2) pull both tails in, with fewer fragment beats and fewer forty-word chains, and many more 9–18-word sentences carrying a clear action; (3) **fewer marked breaks**, with sections running ≈950 words; (4) let vocabulary carry slightly more weight (target grade ≈6.8). Section 8 signals stay secondary ("that" below 92 per 10k; adverbs and dialogue tags moderate; combat vocabulary ≈22 per 10k in the background throughout). Measure after each movement. Paragraph and scene figures are ASR-inferred proxies; development counts are heuristics.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:232:**The source's refrains:** Read the source for events, not sentences. It leans on a handful of refrains: "catalogued," "which was a ledger line," "which from Seln was a whole report," "a stride and a half," "the voice for a distance / an inventory," "filed," "the shelf," "did not have a column for it," and "which was, from X, a paragraph." Keep a few as character signatures (Cael catalogues; Pike reads things twice; a stride and a half is Oryn's distance). Thin the rest hard. Protected lines (§10) are exempt.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:234:**Reader Standard (outranks voice):** clean language, moral clarity, violence with cost and no gore, no innuendo. Carry the source's Gate-27 WATCH notes into the retelling. The ford witness who "got his hand across his own throat somehow" must read unambiguously as *not* self-inflicted (he got his hand between the jaws and his throat). Name the den's remains in one clause. Blood once, as stakes. Cael's decision to read Oryn without consent is named as wrong by him and by three others before it happens.
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:283:- Ch13, the covenant, whole: *Written before. Tomorrow morning, the back room, the door shut. Oryn runs the long reading. Both hands, all of her, all of me, twenty minutes. I lie still. I'm still and whole for the first time in front of her; she said so in the yard, with the tape off.* / *The conditions, as I have them. Sustained: twenty minutes at contact is longer than any bout I've stood. Stakes: I'm three days off the Ring and the nine are still settling; she's three mendings down and her route's late at the far end and she's spending a fourth on a patient who's given her nothing four times. Earnest: she'll do the thing she does as well as she does it. Karis: the model says real, not fight. I don't know if the model's right. Nobody does. Tomorrow's the first time it could be tested and I'm the test.* / *The price. She doesn't know what I am. She can't consent to what she can't know about — not won't; can't. There's nothing I could put in front of her tonight that she could say yes or no to, because the thing doesn't have a name she's heard. I've decided not to tell her before. My reasons are good, and they're the reasons of somebody who wants it, and the real one is that I don't know what she'd say. Entered.* / *If it takes what she's using on me, it takes it from the one person on this road who came to help. I don't know what it costs a source. It's never shown. Tomorrow's the first time it could, and if it does, she pays, and I chose that for her.* / *After: I tell her. In full. On her table, before I'm off it. Whatever it costs me, including the route walking north without me on it.* / *I want it. Write that too.* / *Write it before, not after. That's the whole difference between me and the system.*
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:295:- Ch24, the inventory: *Ten confirmed fragments.* / *Wind-adjacent — Lira. Pressure-adjacent — the Bronze from Ardenmere. Iron-adjacent — Brom. Compression-adjacent — Reydan. Ember-adjacent — Karis. Shadow-adjacent — Seln; source protected; the seal held past the Line as it held inside, and was used twice out here where no one who could carry it west could see it, and that is the seal's whole logic and it is unchanged. Storm-adjacent — Daeva. Anchor-adjacent — unnamed; the hand with no face; opened a door on a rim and held a floor in a hall, and I own a piece of the craft the system uses to hold people and have used it twice this year, once each way. Blade-adjacent — Ephram. Tide-adjacent — Oryn; partial; Iron; self and contact; the tenth, and the first that does nothing in a fight, and the only one whose engagement field says clinical, and the only one with a rule on it in her hand and mine: ask first, every time. Deployment notes current on all ten.* / *One anomaly. Session nine. Tide-adjacent. Not an entry any more; a location. The still place. Read three times. Doesn't flow. Doesn't change. Everything goes around it. Not the Quiet. Not a fragment. Older than the log. Observation continues.* / *Reydan will get his answer. Daeva will get her rematch. Both are going to need a map.* — **Audio rule:** Feryn's name never appears in a list run beside Oryn's; every inventory says "the Bronze from Ardenmere."
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:333:| The Architect / any maker (B8 title; B11; B13–14) | Indefinite agency **only where the source has it**: "A circle is a made shape." (Ch10); "Somebody made a floor that turns Paths off." (Ch15); "Someone made this pattern." (Ch24); "a line … somebody drew before there was a registry" (Ch24). Also "Pike said a handful." | Any who, why, will, intent, reset, list of parts, "Architect," "apparatus," "un-bound" (Book 8's leaf words); any new maker sentence |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:334:| The Quieting's source (Architect reset; B10–11) | Observable mechanics only: perfect circle, about 220 yards [B6-reconciled 2026-10-11: audit A2], sharp line, identical failure, fused floors, carvings, fauna denning | Spread; growth; any city; any change in a site's size |
editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/BOOK_MAP.md:335:| The still place | Located (M6, unnamed); named as *the still place* (M8); read three times; "Not the Quiet. Not a fragment." | *source, before, primordial, recurrence* (Book 9's word); a Rune-like "shape with bones" (Book 8's); any theory, including Oryn's |
