+### Lane A join audit — chapter 1 log
+
+- First seam, sentence before: `Entered, because I can't remember the last person who didn't.`
+- First seam, sentence after: `Under it he added the other.`
+- Second seam, sentence before: `It was getting to be a habit.`
+- Second seam, sentence after: `Deployment since the Line: none.`
+- Ruling: Sound. The narrator can shift from the italic log to narration, then back to the short repeated log line; the two plain-prose sentences make the action and habitual repetition explicit without a broken join.
