editions/monroe-1.3/book-07-void-roads/manuscript/chapter-15.md:5:She had gone up to the eave on purpose to be first. Cael came after her at his own pace, which on level grass was anybody's pace now, and he took his inventory on the way, as he took it at the start of anything. The calf was a leg again on the flat; he had asked it the evening before, on the saddle road, and it had told him nine strides uphill and then shut. Brom's forearm was closed along the whole of its seam and wrapped by Brom's own choice, and it was to pull nothing. Lira had wound a strip of linen round her right ankle, over the stocking, and she walked on the whole sole of that foot. Karis had two pink lines across each palm and held a pencil for a quarter of an hour at a time. The nine fragments lay in him as they had lain since the ford, idle, each with its rent paid.
