+   Last six: `He put it.`  
+   Listening notes: Lira and Brom own the strap dispute; Karis gives the ruling. Cael's four italic paragraphs are a log entry, deployment one. Numerals are spelled out in narration. Clean.
+5. First six: `They left the Thornwater road in`  
+   Last six: `this. It is not a stone."`  
+   Listening notes: Lira prompts the echo; Cael's echoed italic `What` is environmental repetition, not a new speaker. Karis, Seln and Brom are tagged as the terrain comes into view. The closing reply to Lira is Brom's, supported by his position in the immediately preceding paragraph and his trade judgment. Clean.
+
+### Lane A join audit — chapter 15 slope
+
+- Sentence before: `He had slipped the rope from his shoulder, and he stood with his head back and his mouth a little open, looking at two hundred yards and more of stone that would slide if a goat sneezed on it.`
+- Sentence after: `"Can it be done?" said Lira.`
+- Ruling: Sound. The direct question lands cleanly on the revealed slope, and Brom's untagged answer is secured by his preceding inspection and the trade-specific `I've not put my foot on it.`
+
+## Supplementary audit record
+
+- Coverage: all fifteen files were printed whole, in order. Automated scene counts confirm `5, 5, 5, 6, 5, 5, 7, 5, 5, 5, 6, 5, 5, 6, 5`.
+- Quote/italic integrity: every chapter has an even raw count of straight quotation marks and asterisks. The only odd-count paragraphs are the first two paragraphs of Karis's three-paragraph read-aloud hypothesis in chapter 9; the third paragraph supplies the intentional closing quotation mark.
+- Scene-break integrity: every `---` in the range has a blank line before and after.
+- Arabic numerals outside headings: `*Cu 3*` (ch2), `*110 yards*` (ch6), and `*110*` / `*110 yards*` (ch9). The `110` occurrences are visible field-note marks. `Cu 3` is also a visible old rating, but the abbreviation flattens ambiguously for narration; required-fix candidate: `*Copper 3*`.
+- Markdown/forms: no code fences, bracketed forms, or stray backticks occur in chapters 1–15. Initials `L.`, `C.` and `H.` are intentional document/letter forms. `HOLD` is intentional visible board text.
+- Duplicate-word scan: no accidental doubled word. Repeated `had had` forms are grammatical and audible.
+- Long-paragraph scan: eight paragraphs exceed 700 characters; carried into the proof's required list.
+- Proposed-fix validation: both old strings occur exactly once in chapters 1–15, neither is protected, neither proposed new string already occurs, and an in-memory eight-word source comparison found no newly introduced source overlap.
